<title>USA: GOLF-LEADING FINAL SCORES AT THE HAWAIIAN OPEN.</title>
<headline>GOLF-LEADING FINAL SCORES AT THE HAWAIIAN OPEN.</headline>
<dateline>HONOLULU, Hawaii 1997-02-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading scores after</p>
<p>the final round of the $1.2 million United Hawaiian Open on</p>
<p>Sunday at the 7,012-yard, par-72 Waialae C.C. course (players</p>
<p>U.S. unless noted):</p>
<p>271 Paul Stankowski 71 66 64 70, Jim Furyk 70 67 66 68, Mike</p>
<p>Reid 62 72 66 71 (Stankowski won with a birdie on the fourth</p>
<p>hole of sudden death.)</p>
<p>273 Donnie Hammond 70 68 66 69, Jay Don Blake 68 70 66 69</p>
<p>274 Tom Lehman 65 69 69 71</p>
<p>275 Paul Goydos 70 66 71 68, Lee Porter 70 66 67 72</p>
<p>277 Joe Durant 69 69 69 70, Paul Azinger 67 70 69 71, Stuart</p>
<p>Appleby (Australia) 67 70 69 71, Taylor Smith 72 66 68 71</p>
<p>278 Tom Byrum 67 70 71 70, Peter Jordan 63 70 73 72, Brian</p>
<p>Claar 62 75 69 72, Craig Stadler 71 66 72 69, Scott Simpson 65</p>
<p>66 74 73, Brad Bryant 68 71 71 68</p>
<p>278 Shane Bertsch 68 67 72 72, Brent Geiberger 69 69 68 73,</p>
<p>John Maginnes 68 67 71 73, Bruce Fleisher 70 68 68 73, Doug</p>
<p>Barron 67 69 69 74, Ed Dougherty 64 69 71 75, Len Mattiace 64</p>
<p>70 69 76, Tim Herron 66 70 68 75</p>
<p>Additional regional scores</p>
<p>285 Hideki Kase (Japan) 71 69 70 75</p>
<p>286 Nobuo Serizawa (Japan) 70 66 72 78</p>
</text>
